  async plan(world){const schema=creationPlanSchema(world.printRequirements||[]),allowed=Object.entries(creationPairs(world.printRequirements||[])).flatMap(([kind,uses])=>uses.map(use=>kind+'/'+use)).join(', ');const prompt=`Current creation step: ${world.printIntent||world.objective}. Whole objective for context: ${world.objective}. Required later interactions for this object: ${JSON.stringify(world.printRequirements||[])}. Character context: ${world.stateForModel?.()||world.actorName||""}\nPropose 2 or 3 concrete useful object plans to achieve this goal. Each label describes the object AND its behavior. Choose only these compatible kind/interaction pairs for this object: ${allowed}. A squishy plush or soft landing pad MUST use soft/squish, never a rigid prop/store. Working cars MUST use vehicle/drive. A seat needs prop/sit. A shower requires prop/wash, anchored with a low accessible tray and an overhead outlet above the 2.3m character. A bed or resting platform MUST use prop/rest: the engine supports lying down to recover energy. It does not simulate a sleep cycle. All plans may share a kind but offer different functional designs. IDs a,b,c. Never force storage unless storing things is part of the goal. Edible foods are prop/display with food material and edible attributes; eating is an object action, not a storage affordance. Use prop/store only if the current creation is explicitly a container or a later use/store step requires it. A small fruit is not a storage device. All proposals MUST preserve explicit species, color and function, such as red panda (animal with rust coat, pale facial markings and ringed tail). Only supported behaviors can be promised. Previous rejected plan reason: ${world.planRejection||"none"}. Correct it.`;return {prompt,...await this.generate('You are a creative physical-object planner in a small garden. Propose feasible executable plans, not fabricated world facts. The selection-only actor will choose one.',prompt,schema,750)};}
